<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP's raw steel output falls in Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP's raw steel output falls in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd, Australia's only significant steel producer, said raw steel output fell 7.2 percent in October with the decline mainly due to a production fall at the Newcastle works north of Sydney.</p>
<p>BHP said all other centres achieved good production, with total despatches up six percent in the latest month.</p>
<p>&quot;An increase in New Zealand despatches is largely the result of timing issues,&quot; it said in its monthly production report.</p>
<p>&quot;Despatches from other international operations increased 22 percent for the five months to October due mainly to increased capacity in the U.S. and South East Asia.&quot;  </p>
